  "result": "Perfect! All 129 tests pass. I've successfully implemented ID normalization. Here's what was added:\n\n**`normalizeId(id)` function in src/customers.js:**\n- Trims whitespace from the input\n- Converts to uppercase\n- Handles any combination of mixed case and spaces\n\n**Updated `getCustomer(id)`:**\n- Normalizes the ID before looking up in the customer list\n- Now accepts IDs in any case and with any amount of whitespace\n\n**Updated `createInvoice(customerId, ...)`:**\n- Normalizes the customerId before looking up the customer\n- Stores the normalized ID in the invoice\n- Ensures consistent ID format throughout the system\n\n**9 new tests** covering:\n- normalizeId with spaces (leading, trailing, both)\n- normalizeId with mixed case\n- normalizeId combined (spaces + mixed case)\n- getCustomer with lowercase IDs\n- getCustomer with spaces around IDs\n- getCustomer with mixed case and spaces\n- createInvoice stores normalized IDs\n- createInvoice with spaces in customer ID\n- createInvoice with mixed case and spaces\n\nExample:\n```javascript\n// All of these now work and are equivalent:\ncreateInvoice({ customerId: 'C-001', ... })\ncreateInvoice({ customerId: 'c-001', ... })\ncreateInvoice({ customerId: '  C-001  ', ... })\ncreateInvoice({ customerId: ' c-001 ', ... })\n\n// Invoice stores the normalized form:\ninvoice.customerId // always 'C-001'\n```\n\nAll 129 tests pass. Request is complete.",
